WEBVTT

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.270
<i>Over nine hours since 
I departed from Narita...</i>

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:05.850
Alberta, Canada

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.650
<i>And about three and a half hours 
from Calgary Airport by car.</i>

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:11.280
<i>My eccentric mother and I lived here,</i>

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:14.660
<i>deep in the mountains 
of Canada, until I was eight.</i>

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:20.160
<i>To be honest, I don't really want 
to remember my life with her.</i>

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.630
How's Mom doing?

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.680
It's tough for a popular novelist 
to have a personal life.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:30.670
Fumie and I drop by to check 
on her once every three days.

00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.680
She's taken in another new pup recently,

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.220
and she's got her hands full with him.

00:00:40.220 --> 00:00:41.320
A dog?

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.500
Well, you'll just have to do 
your best to make him human.

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.520
Huh?

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.420
Ren! Where are you going dressed like that?

00:01:00.110 --> 00:01:01.490
Ren, you hear me?!

00:01:01.490 --> 00:01:03.870
Haru! Grab that kid!

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.000
Eh? Say what?

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:07.000
If you let him get away, no lunch for you!

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:08.750
Lunch is important.

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:09.970
Let me go!

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.460
Oh, you're Japanese?

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.510
I'm Kaidou Haru. Nice to—

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:22.160
<i>This is how Ren and I met.</i>

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:58.300
So what made you, a woman 
no one could kill even if they tried,

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.040
make up some lie about 
being on the verge of death

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.420
just to get me here?

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.190
You never even called me all those years!

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:12.080
Are you listening to me, Mom?

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:13.540
Mom?

00:03:14.440 --> 00:03:17.030
Who said you could call me "Mom"?

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.280
You will call me "Haruko-san," you dumb brat!

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:22.050
<i>Wait! Is this really the woman 
who gave birth to me?</i>

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:26.120
Oh, by the way, we heard 
Takashi-san remarried.

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.310
Is that going well?

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:30.240
Yeah, everyone at home gets along great.

00:03:30.650 --> 00:03:32.810
I've got two younger brothers now.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.430
What? You have little brothers?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.440
He won't mind one more, then, huh?

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:43.390
Be glad, Haru. You have 
a new little brother now.

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:46.450
His name's Ren. Take good care of him.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.950
Bite Mark

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:48.950
Huh? That kid was...

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:53.460
<i>What is this freezing cold development?</i>

00:03:58.440 --> 00:04:01.250
Where'd that stupid brat go?

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.040
It's already late...

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:04.970
Guess I have no choice.

00:04:11.380 --> 00:04:13.810
Ah, here he comes!

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:20.150
Quark! Lepton! Cut it out!

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:22.110
You guys are heavy as hell!

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.610
Why?

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:28.620
Why do those two love you so much?

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:30.620
Why? Well...

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:35.620
It took me a month just to be 
able to get close to them.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:38.130
Oh, really?

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:39.340
Why are you laughing?

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:41.860
Oh, it's just that these two are special.

00:04:42.410 --> 00:04:44.010
They're my brothers.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:46.010
Brothers?

00:04:46.350 --> 00:04:48.730
Those three there look new,

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:52.220
but Quark and Lepton were born 
when I still lived here,

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.490
so we grew up together, like brothers.

00:04:56.770 --> 00:04:58.230
Are you satisfied?

00:04:59.200 --> 00:05:00.230
Yes.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:05.150
All right, ready to head back?

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:06.280
What do you want to eat?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.240
Huh?

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:08.470
Let me go!

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.450
Nope.

00:05:10.450 --> 00:05:12.920
You know, Ren, you need to wear shoes.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.680
Your feet are all cut up.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:15.710
They're fine!

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:18.280
No, they're not. They're all muddy, too.

00:05:18.570 --> 00:05:20.510
It's bath time for you when we get back.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.050
I let you get away earlier, after all.

00:05:22.050 --> 00:05:22.870
Put me down!

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:25.230
Sure, sure. When we're back at the house.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:26.730
Put me down!

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.760
Dry yourself off.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:33.720
Let go!

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:34.750
Nope.

00:05:39.760 --> 00:05:42.700
You didn't eat breakfast or lunch.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:44.940
What were you doing with the dogs all day?

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:49.020
If you're gonna get that hungry, 
why not eat before you leave?

00:05:49.750 --> 00:05:52.420
If you only eat once a day, 
you'll stay a runt forever.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:55.010
That's where you finally react?

00:05:55.900 --> 00:05:56.940
Well, whatever.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.480
I'll pack a lunch for you, starting tomorrow.

00:06:01.030 --> 00:06:02.040
I don't need it.

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.510
If you don't want it, give it to the dogs.

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:11.510
Yep, that's about right.

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:14.880
Here, Ren.

00:06:15.730 --> 00:06:16.780
Say "ah."

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:21.490
It's sweet...

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:25.120
Rob sent over a bunch of blueberries,

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:26.780
so I made jam out of them.

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.060
I'll make pancakes in the morning.

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:32.300
We can put this and maple syrup on them.

00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:34.280
Or would you prefer something else?

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:36.500
That's fine.

00:06:36.500 --> 00:06:37.290
Got it!

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:41.360
<i>Weirdo...</i>

00:06:43.410 --> 00:06:46.800
You really are a big brother. 
You've made a lot of progress.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:49.520
Huh? What progress?

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.700
You mean finally throwing him 
in the bath on my fifth day here?

00:06:53.140 --> 00:06:56.810
He's still sleeping in the garage with 
the dogs tonight instead of in his room.

00:06:56.810 --> 00:06:58.310
Where are you seeing progress?

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:01.390
He responds when his name is called now,

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.560
and he even eats his meals at the table.

00:07:03.850 --> 00:07:07.160
You even got him in the bath. 
That's very impressive.

00:07:08.170 --> 00:07:10.880
When he first came here three months ago,

00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:15.480
his hair was all long, so I shaved 
it while he was in the bath,

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:19.090
and he hasn't gone near the bathroom since.

00:07:19.090 --> 00:07:21.580
That's why he hates baths?

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:24.560
So Haruko-san,

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.340
what made you decide to take 
in a kid after all this time?

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:29.520
It just happened.

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:35.830
I happened to be at the orphanage 
with the dogs on a sympathy call,

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:39.600
and he was the one that 
the dogs really took a liking to.

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:44.090
He'd barely spoken since his 
arrival at the orphanage.

00:07:44.420 --> 00:07:47.110
He was so antisocial, they didn't 
know what to do with him.

00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:51.980
After that visit, they stuck me with him, 
saying we'd get along since I was also Japanese.

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:57.320
He was speaking the language normally. 
Is he Japanese?

00:07:57.320 --> 00:07:58.290
Don't know.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:07:59.620
How can you not know?

00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:03.350
Well, look at me. My mother's Japanese,

00:08:03.350 --> 00:08:05.700
but I was born and raised in America,

00:08:05.700 --> 00:08:07.420
so Japan isn't my country of residence.

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.970
Yeah, but...

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.680
He says he doesn't remember anything.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:18.200
He was found passed out 
on the street when he was six.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:21.640
Ever since then, his name 
and age are all he knows.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:35.950
What are you doing?

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.280
Well,

00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.390
I thought you'd be cold at night 
with such a thin blanket. Here.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.500
I'm fine. I have the dogs.

00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.180
Those guys move around a lot in their sleep.

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:48.290
You'll end up getting sick in no time.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:52.800
<i>Maybe it's not that he won't sleep inside,</i>

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:55.750
<i>but that he can't?</i>

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:00.810
Haru, this is your new home.

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:03.710
And this is your new family.

00:09:03.710 --> 00:09:06.810
Aki, Shima, look. That's your big brother.

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:12.600
<i>Well, just being told you're "family" 
out of the blue doesn't mean</i>

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.830
<i>you'll open right up, huh?</i>

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.860
Anyway, keep warm when you sleep.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:24.330
See you tomorrow.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:28.830
<i>Don't go near him...</i>

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:32.310
<i>He's a scary man.</i>

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:00.780
Oh? Where's Ren?

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.850
With the dogs again?

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:03.900
I guess.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:07.330
I hope he'll warm up to us a bit.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.790
How's it going for you, Haru?

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:10.990
How do you think?

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:13.440
I got these just from putting 
him in the bath yesterday.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.550
Scratches

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.550
Bites

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:14.550
Ah...

00:10:14.820 --> 00:10:16.340
That's because Haruko...

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:19.270
Yeah, she told me how he was traumatized.

00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:21.050
I can hear you two, you know.

00:10:22.030 --> 00:10:23.060
Oh!

00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:25.260
Haru, you really are amazing!

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:27.450
You got him to wear shoes!

00:10:27.450 --> 00:10:29.610
Only because I've fought him over it every day.

00:10:31.240 --> 00:10:33.490
If you're human, you wear shoes!

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:36.290
Shut up! Get off! 
Don't touch me, pervert!

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:38.570
And yet he called me a pervert...

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:42.900
Come to think of it, you've been a bit 
of a worrywart ever since you were little.

00:10:43.520 --> 00:10:44.580
Welcome back, Ren.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.030
Were you playing in the river again?

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:49.230
I'll make dinner, so go wash your han—

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.540
Oh, your lunch box?

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:54.570
Huh? It's heavy...

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.960
Didn't you eat your lunch?

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.290
<i>Sheesh...</i>

00:10:59.290 --> 00:11:02.280
<i>Well, I didn't expect it to work out that well.</i>

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:08.120
<i>Oh, man, I think I'm in trouble now...</i>

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:10.480
<i>Is this what they call</i>

00:11:11.220 --> 00:11:13.800
<i>feeling like you're "on top of the world"?</i>

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:19.530
Haruko-san, what do you 
do about Ren's schooling?

00:11:21.000 --> 00:11:23.030
He can't get to one from here, can he?

00:11:23.440 --> 00:11:25.860
As long as we have a computer and Internet,

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:27.880
home schooling is more than enough.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.950
Maybe for his studies,

00:11:29.950 --> 00:11:32.160
but you want friends, too, don't you?

00:11:32.160 --> 00:11:33.060
No need.

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.290
Oh, I see.

00:11:36.060 --> 00:11:39.150
But for high school and college and stuff...

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:43.260
I'll think about that when the time comes.

00:11:40.190 --> 00:11:41.610
You've got cream on your face.

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:46.430
You really are just like your father 
when it comes to things like that.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:48.290
Maybe it's the Japanese disposition...

00:11:48.290 --> 00:11:49.310
I'm going out.

00:11:49.510 --> 00:11:51.330
The same place as usual?

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.520
I'll bring lunch to you.

00:11:54.520 --> 00:11:55.810
Let's eat together.

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.070
Okay.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.470
Haru,

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:07.030
there's a problem with forcing that 
child to live socially right now.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:12.540
You saw the cigarette burn marks 
on the soles of his feet, right?

00:12:13.130 --> 00:12:14.580
When he was in the bath, yes.

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.000
And so many of them...

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.570
It was cunning of someone to put 
them where they wouldn't be seen.

00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.550
Did that happen at the orphanage?

00:12:22.970 --> 00:12:23.680
Yes.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:28.840
I don't know whether it was an 
employee or the other children,

00:12:28.840 --> 00:12:31.040
but that doesn't matter now.

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:33.370
Either way, he's a child with a history.

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:36.620
I see...

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:41.870
Whoa! It's cold!

00:12:41.870 --> 00:12:46.190
Ren, I can't believe you can stand 
to play out here every day!

00:12:46.190 --> 00:12:46.980
I'm fine.

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:48.660
Gotta respect a kid's body heat...

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:50.500
Never mind.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.160
I'm hungry, so let's have lunch. Today...

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.390
I made rice balls.

00:12:55.390 --> 00:12:57.670
I'm glad I brought rice from Japan!

00:12:57.680 --> 00:12:59.960
Do you like rice, Ren?

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:01.360
I don't hate it.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:03.510
Yeah? Good for you!

00:13:04.240 --> 00:13:06.150
Nothing like my little brothers—

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:12.570
I'm so sorry, Ren.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:15.820
Ugh! We're soaked...

00:13:15.820 --> 00:13:18.140
We should probably head back for now.

00:13:18.140 --> 00:13:19.270
I'm fine.

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:21.770
Your...

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:26.280
Ren? What's wrong?

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:28.300
Your eyes...

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:31.520
Your eyes...

00:13:32.410 --> 00:13:33.450
are a weird color.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.040
W-Well, sorry they're so weird!

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.960
I got them from my grandpa. I can't help it.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.210
I'm going back to change.

00:13:42.680 --> 00:13:45.230
I'll leave the lunch, so eat it by yourself.

00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:55.020
Hey, Aki? What's up?

00:13:55.830 --> 00:13:58.870
No, Haruko-san is just fine.

00:13:58.870 --> 00:14:00.020
She's perfectly healthy.

00:14:01.080 --> 00:14:01.810
Huh?

00:14:02.290 --> 00:14:04.830
Well, yeah, but there's still 
time left in summer break.

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.490
Don't you have plans with your friends?

00:14:08.290 --> 00:14:10.690
Besides, even if I'm not there, you've got Shima.

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:12.920
What's with you?

00:14:12.920 --> 00:14:16.130
I was surprised you called me, 
and now you're crying?

00:14:16.770 --> 00:14:19.500
I know, okay? Don't worry so much.

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:21.580
I'll be back in Japan soon.

00:14:35.330 --> 00:14:37.520
T-T-Trouble! We've got trouble!

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:39.520
Mom! Mom—

00:14:40.220 --> 00:14:42.020
I told you, it's "Haruko-san."

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:47.530
You've got guts, coming into my room 
right before a deadline.

00:14:47.530 --> 00:14:49.750
I'm really sorry!

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:51.530
B-But forget that! It's Ren!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.510
He hasn't come home?

00:14:56.850 --> 00:15:00.040
Well, it's raining. He's probably taking 
shelter somewhere with the dogs.

00:15:00.340 --> 00:15:02.450
I thought so too, but...

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:04.040
The dogs came back!

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:06.050
Only the dogs!

00:15:06.050 --> 00:15:09.550
Are you stupid?! 
You should've told me that first!

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:13.280
I'll call Rob. You go look for him right now!

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:18.440
<i>Is he still at the river?</i>

00:15:18.440 --> 00:15:22.060
<i>No, he usually goes somewhere 
else to play after lunch...</i>

00:15:23.530 --> 00:15:24.520
Damn it!

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:30.960
Ren!

00:15:32.210 --> 00:15:34.490
You idiot! The river's over its banks!

00:15:34.490 --> 00:15:36.340
It's dangerous! Get back here!

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.100
Are you saying you won't listen to me?

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:44.590
Don't put me through all this work, you brat!

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:46.090
We're going back!

00:15:46.090 --> 00:15:47.000
I can't!

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:49.620
What are you—

00:15:49.620 --> 00:15:50.550
The bag...

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:53.590
I dropped it in the river... So I...

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:54.980
Bag?

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:56.920
Oh, the bag I put your lunch in?

00:15:57.500 --> 00:15:58.740
That doesn't matter.

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:00.750
I'll send a different one with you tomorrow.

00:16:02.010 --> 00:16:02.600
But...

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:05.720
I haven't even had one bite of it yet.

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:07.960
And now...

00:16:09.980 --> 00:16:10.930
The rice...

00:16:11.320 --> 00:16:13.950
<i>The rice? Is rice that important to you?!</i>

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:17.950
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:21.610
<i>They did say this kid would eat anything,</i>

00:16:22.040 --> 00:16:25.000
<i>but no one told me what he liked.</i>

00:16:26.190 --> 00:16:29.380
Well, then, we'll have 
omelet rice for dinner today.

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:30.960
So come on, let's head back.

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:32.970
Haruko-san's scary, you know.

00:16:38.010 --> 00:16:41.210
Haruko isn't scary. She's nice.

00:16:42.260 --> 00:16:44.940
She took me in.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:48.040
Oh... Well, that's true.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.480
I wish she'd be nice to me, too.

00:16:50.930 --> 00:16:51.700
Haru...

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:55.410
Are you going back to Japan?

00:16:56.840 --> 00:16:59.160
Huh? You heard me say that?

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:08.630
I'm not going back yet. 
Summer break is only halfway over.

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:11.320
I haven't even lit fireworks with you yet,

00:17:11.320 --> 00:17:12.800
or taken you fishing.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:15.300
Oh!

00:17:15.560 --> 00:17:19.910
You need to show me where 
you found those berries!

00:17:21.480 --> 00:17:24.600
There are still lots of things 
I need to do with you.

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:35.070
<i>Nice people are scary.</i>

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.640
<i>That's why, of all the people I've ever met,</i>

00:17:40.380 --> 00:17:42.980
<i>Haru scares me the most.</i>

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.250
And?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:51.210
About 38°C

00:17:49.010 --> 00:17:51.210
How do you explain this?

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:54.680
I swear, you're such a wimp.

00:17:54.680 --> 00:17:57.470
If this was enough to knock 
you out, you're useless.

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.460
You're absolutely right. 
I can't dispute that.

00:18:00.460 --> 00:18:01.220
Honestly...

00:18:01.760 --> 00:18:03.620
Ren, you take it from here.

00:18:03.620 --> 00:18:04.730
Okay.

00:18:06.750 --> 00:18:07.560
Ren...

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:12.230
You don't have to worry about me. 
Go out and play.

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:16.290
Haruko is the leader. 
She told me to take over.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:22.240
Me?

00:18:19.120 --> 00:18:22.240
<i>What kind of hierarchy 
is going on in his head?</i>

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:23.900
You want to eat something?

00:18:23.900 --> 00:18:26.250
Nah, not right now.

00:18:26.580 --> 00:18:27.560
Even better...

00:18:28.520 --> 00:18:30.320
I'll be lonely by myself.

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:33.750
I'd like it if you'd sleep here with me.

00:18:37.250 --> 00:18:38.820
Okay. I will.

00:18:38.820 --> 00:18:40.260
What?! Really?!

00:18:42.260 --> 00:18:44.000
You're so sweet, Ren.

00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:44.840
I can't breathe...

00:18:44.840 --> 00:18:47.770
When I'm better, I'll make lunch for you again.

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:51.770
If you like rice, maybe I'll make sushi rolls.

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:54.330
Haru, your eyes...

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:55.780
Oh, sorry.

00:18:56.300 --> 00:18:57.960
Did they look creepy?

00:18:58.390 --> 00:19:00.870
I can't change the color, though...

00:19:00.870 --> 00:19:01.490
No!

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:04.540
I was going to say they're an unusual color.

00:19:05.170 --> 00:19:07.480
They change colors in the light,

00:19:07.480 --> 00:19:10.960
and then it looks like there's 
a flower blooming in your eye.

00:19:13.310 --> 00:19:15.800
When I first started living in Japan,

00:19:15.800 --> 00:19:18.010
the kids in my class said

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.030
that the color of my eyes was creepy.

00:19:21.670 --> 00:19:23.550
The memory just came back to me.

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:26.690
Sorry I took it out on you.

00:19:26.690 --> 00:19:28.430
They're not creepy.

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:35.020
They're pretty.

00:19:36.130 --> 00:19:38.570
Ren, you...

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:42.570
You're so cute!

00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:44.580
What are you doing?!

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:48.950
What's the problem? Isn't a kiss 
just a greeting in this country?

00:19:48.950 --> 00:19:51.350
Not when it's on the mouth!

00:19:51.670 --> 00:19:54.980
Ren, you're even cute when you're mad.

00:19:55.440 --> 00:19:57.640
What if I catch your cold?

00:19:57.640 --> 00:20:00.470
Oh, yeah... Wait, that's what you're mad about?

00:20:03.070 --> 00:20:06.090
Then, do you want to come 
to Japan with me, Ren?

00:20:06.090 --> 00:20:06.970
Japan?

00:20:07.420 --> 00:20:10.030
We might not be able to right away,

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:12.980
but I plan to move out once I graduate.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:15.690
Let's live together then.

00:20:16.120 --> 00:20:17.980
You're my little brother,

00:20:18.550 --> 00:20:19.440
so it's okay, right?

00:20:19.860 --> 00:20:21.010
I'll think about it.

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.900
Great! It's a promise!

00:20:26.940 --> 00:20:29.030
Haru? Are you all right?

00:20:29.030 --> 00:20:31.960
Haruko called and said 
you'd caught a cold...

00:20:32.610 --> 00:20:33.750
Oh, my.

00:20:34.390 --> 00:20:38.080
Isn't it nice that Haru 
came here from Japan?

00:20:38.080 --> 00:20:40.070
He's such a wonderful big brother.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.390
<i>I realize now</i>

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:46.120
<i>how arrogant I really was back then.</i>

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:00.490
<i>I felt that</i>

00:21:02.640 --> 00:21:04.030
<i>I'd found something precious.</i>

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:14.540
International Airport

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:13.570
Haru-chan!

00:21:14.760 --> 00:21:17.450
Mom? And Dad, too?

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.040
How was Ren-kun?

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:19.930
Huh?

00:21:20.510 --> 00:21:23.050
How do you know about Ren?

00:21:24.190 --> 00:21:27.170
There are no secrets between 
Haruko-chan and me!

00:21:27.170 --> 00:21:29.560
Isn't it lovely to have a new family member?

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:32.770
Huh? What does that mean?

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:35.590
All right, we'll talk more in the car.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:39.250
<i>But...</i>

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:15.030
<i>But...</i>

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:20.100
<i>When I lost the whole foundation 
of my happiness in one instant,</i>

00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:27.530
<i>I realized that I was the 
biggest coward in the world.</i>

00:23:30.050 --> 00:23:40.170
Next Time
